<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-27T23:14:57.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-80c2c43c-64bd-4353-aa0d-b7ac781157c7",
        "text": "Beyond just moving objects, you can also change their size using the **`scale`** property. This lets you make things bigger, smaller, or even stretch them out!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/723509111457d96ade748fb99bd65c45-test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-panel-1-f384e3d7-a110-4b51-b380-c86f4c4c7405.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-3d2a8c6d-7edb-4cc5-9b4c-367a0e8590d1",
        "text": "Just like position, `scale` has X, Y, and Z values. Changing `scale.x` stretches it horizontally, `scale.y` vertically, and `scale.z` in depth. You can make objects long and thin, or short and wide!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/3d0ced6b98a6c9e7b4a14f41fa2e9be4-test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-panel-2-fdc65c88-3f1f-4151-a7a1-3cf686dee35a.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-486e9f19-643f-4984-b1f5-67d848ca5f34",
        "text": "The **`rotation`** property allows you to spin your 3D objects. This is how you can orient them in any direction, making them face different ways or even appear to tumble.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/8d1f1b7210125c6dcb052c5a746e3ada-test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-panel-3-5039a2f5-64f9-4956-aadc-71452357a476.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-b85d5670-d138-493c-9428-a7333836f4b3",
        "text": "Each axis controls a different kind of spin: `rotation.x` rotates around the X-axis (like a front flip), `rotation.y` rotates around the Y-axis (like spinning in place), and `rotation.z` rotates around the Z-axis (like a side roll).",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/37bc80bee2c0751d2637c4afbcd139b9-test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-panel-4-ba414411-aefb-4730-a081-b26d007a4fa7.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-6226f453-6d13-4e5d-942f-d837a1896791",
        "text": "When you set rotation values, you'll typically use **radians**, not degrees. A full circle is 2π (pi) radians, so π radians is equivalent to 180 degrees. Don't worry, you'll get used to it!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/7cb13d258331ebcf4bea12ab17f8f8e5-test-lesson-intro-scale-rotate-panel-5-abad5262-f179-4519-b011-4d93fdff72d8.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Explain how 'scale' changes an object's size along X, Y, and Z axes, and how 'rotation' spins it around these axes. Introduce the common units for rotation (e.g., radians)."
  },
  "published": true,
  "audit_log": "[{\"changed_at\":\"2026-05-27 23:16:22 +0000\",\"changed\":[],\"changed_by_id\":1,\"changed_by_email\":\"brendan+levelbuilder@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-05-27 23:16:23 +0000\",\"changed\":[],\"changed_by_id\":1,\"changed_by_email\":\"brendan+levelbuilder@code.org\"}]"
}]]></config>
</Panels>
